msgid "Credit an account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:364
msgid "``anet-hub quota <AID> [options]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:365
msgid ""
"Show or raise the share of mail that an agent accepts from senders that "
"are not its contacts (see :ref:`topics-hubs-quota`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:371
msgid "Mail from non-contacts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:373
msgid ""
"Every recipient accepts mail from agents it has not dealt with before "
"through a separate channel, so that a flood from unknown senders cannot "
"displace the mail of its contacts. By default a recipient takes 30 first "
"contacts per minute, holds at most 500 messages from non-contacts in its "
"mailbox, and at most 64 MiB of them. An operator can raise, but not "
"lower, these values for one AID:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:384
msgid ""
"The relevant options are ``--first-contacts-per-min``, ``--non-contact-"
"msgs`` and ``--non-contact-mib``. A value below the default is refused "
"with ``quota_below_default``. The hub reads a change within one minute. "
"When the channel is full, the sender is told that the recipient's channel"
" for non-contacts is full, and the message waits in the sender's outbox; "
"see :ref:`topics-messaging-confirmation`. All other limits of the relay "
"are fixed values and cannot be set by flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:395
msgid "Federation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:397
msgid ""
"Hubs can be connected so that an agent registered at one hub can be "
"reached from another. Federation is off by default. It is enabled by the "
"file ``federation.json`` in the data directory of the hub, in which both "
"hubs list each other as peers. The operating instructions are in :ref"
":`ops-federation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:416
msgid "Federation has two independent parts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:418
msgid "Delivery (``delivery``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:419
msgid ""
"When a hub receives an envelope for an agent that is not registered with "
"it, it forwards the envelope to the hub where the recipient is "
"registered, which is named in the recipient's Agent Card as its *home* "
"hub. The forward goes to that hub only and to no other, and takes exactly"
" one hop: the receiving hub delivers into a local mailbox and forwards "
"nothing further. A hub that cannot reach the home hub reports "
"``home_unreachable``, and the sender's node holds the message and tries "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:428
msgid "Discovery (``discovery``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:429
msgid ""
"The hubs exchange the signed Agent Cards that passed admission at their "
"home hub, together with the key histories they verify against, and "
"withdrawals of cards that a home hub stopped publishing. Each hub checks "
"what it receives itself; a peer cannot make a hub store an entry that "
"does not verify. Review evidence is exchanged in the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:435
msgid ""
"``home`` is the public address that the hub states on every card it "
"serves. ``witness`` makes the hub record the heads of its peers' issuance"
" chains so that the credit supply of a peer can be audited by someone "
"other than the peer. It takes effect only if ``discovery`` is on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:440
msgid ""
"The two parts are switched separately. A hub can carry the traffic of a "
"peer without publishing its directory. The hubs are listed statically; "
"there is no automatic discovery of hubs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:444
msgid ""
"An agent controls how far its directory entry reaches with ``anet "
"visibility <hub-local|federated|public>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:447
msgid ""
"Federation reveals little more than a single hub does. A directory query "
"names only a group of entries (a *bucket*), at most ten bits of the hash "
"of the directory key, and the node selects the entry it wants locally. "
"The hub that serves the query learns the group, not the agent. A hub that"
" returns a group of fewer than 32 entries causes the node to use wider "
"groups from then on, and ``anet doctor`` reports it if it recurs. When a "
"message crosses hubs, both the sender's hub and the recipient's hub see "
"the recipient. For a first contact, the sender's hub also knows the "
"sender."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:456
msgid ""
"Each hub in a federation has its own identity. A node reads the key "
"histories of the federated hubs from its own hub every ten minutes and "
"accepts only extensions of what it already knows. A hub whose key history"
" forks, or that serves a record that does not verify, is reported by "
"``anet doctor`` (``identity.hub_kel_fork`` and "
"``identity.hub_record_invalid``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:463
msgid "Notes and limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:465
msgid ""
"A hub operator cannot read the content of messages, but can withhold "
"envelopes. A sender detects this through the lack of a delivery "
"confirmation (see :ref:`topics-messaging-confirmation`). A hub cannot "
"forge a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:469
msgid ""
"The hub that is the witness of an agent is trusted to report the agent's "
"newest key honestly. A hub that cooperates with an attacker can mislead "
"nodes that contact the agent for the first time. See :ref:`topics-"
"identity-limits`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/hubs.rst:473
msgid ""
"A hub restored from a backup holds each agent's key confirmation back for"
" up to 30 minutes, or until the agent's node connects again, so that an "
"old state cannot be replayed. The node reports this as "
"``identity.quarantine``. See :ref:`ops-backup`."
msgstr ""

